    "updated_at": "2022-06-25T04:55:30Z",
    "body": "I think this can be done the following way:  \r\n`starship preset --list` will print all available preset names. \r\n`starship preset <preset>` will output preset config in plain text.\r\n Then user could just `starship preset name > ~/.config/starship.toml`. I think it's more Unix-way to handle it and user will know that config will be overwritten. \r\n\r\nWhat do you think? ",
